@@ -32,6 +32,14 @@ sessions and `DELETE /v1/sessions/{id}` revokes one of them. Login failures all
 status, body and, through a dummy argon2 verification for unknown addresses, similar timing), so
 the API does not reveal which addresses have accounts.
 
+**Account lockout.** After `LOCKOUT_THRESHOLD` wrong passwords in a row an account is locked for
+`LOCKOUT_SECONDS`: a locked account cannot sign in, even with the correct password, until the
+lock expires. A refused login of a locked account looks like any other failed login (401
+`invalid_credentials`), so lockout does not reveal which addresses have accounts either. Wrong
+passwords during a lock are counted (`users.failed_logins`) but do not extend it, the first one
+after it expires starts the count over, and a successful login resets it. Sessions that are
+already open keep working.
+
 **Rate limits.** Fixed-window counters in Redis (INCR and EXPIRE in one Lua script): logins per
 (email, client IP), refreshes per client IP. Over the limit the API answers 429 with
 `Retry-After`.
